## Context
Exposed by the fifth smelt (PR #2049), Commission page open questions
(`memory/topics/commission.md`). Filed under the smelt rule "ticket every
exposed contradiction" (SMELT.md v8-r5). Earlier mentions as evidence or
example only: tickets 1349, 1351.

Claim A, native note `feedback_prose_edits_are_on_main` (Claude Code
auto-memory of the harness, 2026-10-26), quoting the author: "Next time we
should remember that editing prose is on main." How to apply: the author's
hand edits of skill or rule text go in the primary checkout on main, no PR,
review or gate unless asked.

Claim B, `rules/git.md` § Branch and commit: "Main is read-only. Everything
(code, docs, tickets, STATE, memory, config) lands via branch + merge request.
Sole exception: manuscript prose". `rules/prose/workpackages.md`: "The harness
repo keeps its no-exceptions gate."

The note itself says the rule and the preference disagree. The main guard
(`idh.mainGuard`, enforce since 2026-10-27) may refuse such commits.

## Question for the author
Do the author's own hand edits of harness skill or rule text go on main, or
through the gate? Smelt picks no side.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The author's answer is recorded here
- [ ] The losing claim is withdrawn from its store, or the rule is changed by an explicit request naming it
